This product runs on and includes work from:

- ArWen / gpuwm (FahrenheitResearch), the GPU port of the WRF-ARW dynamical core and physics that does the
  atmosphere. Apache License 2.0. Installed by Setup.cmd as the "gpuwm" package (not included in this source);
  its own LICENSE and third-party notices ship with it.
- The Weather Research and Forecasting model (WRF), NCAR / UCAR, which ArWen ports.

Map and ground data in data/ (each folder's SOURCES.md has the details and download links):

- US Census Bureau cartographic boundaries and incorporated places (public domain, 17 U.S.C. 105).
- Natural Earth (public domain).
- GMTED2010 terrain, USGS / NGA (public domain).
- MODIS land use (WRF's WPS_GEOG modis_landuse_20class_30s, NCAR / UCAR; NASA MODIS data, free of restrictions).
- Iowa Environmental Mesonet station list (Iowa State University).

Map tiles fetched while running (not included; attribution is drawn on the map):

- OpenStreetMap tiles, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL), tile.openstreetmap.org under its tile usage policy.
- Esri World Imagery and World Reference layers, (c) Esri, Maxar, Earthstar Geographics, and the GIS User Community.

The 3-D view's landscape, fetched while running (not included):
- ESA WorldCover 10 m 2021 v200, (c) ESA WorldCover project 2021 / Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data
  (2021) processed by ESA WorldCover consortium (CC BY 4.0).
- Roads from OpenStreetMap, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL), through the Overpass API.

Chase mode:
- web/js/chase/world/ (the Detailed map) is built by tools/world/build_world.py from OpenDrive (formerly
  "Real Roads Drive"), a single-page driving world made by a friend of the author.
- Car models: Kenney's Car Kit 3.1 (www.kenney.nl), Creative Commons Zero (CC0) 1.0.
- three.js (MIT License, (c) three.js authors) and earcut (ISC License, (c) Mapbox), loaded from jsDelivr.
- Fetched while running (not included): FEMA USA Structures (public domain, U.S. Government); OpenFreeMap vector
  tiles ((c) OpenMapTiles, data (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL); AWS Terrain Tiles (Mapzen terrarium: SRTM,
  GMTED, NED, ETOPO and others); NAIP and Sentinel-2 imagery and USDA Cropland Data Layer through Microsoft's
  Planetary Computer; ESA WorldCover (CC BY 4.0); Poly Haven textures (CC0).
